export anchor PassportStampsStyle:
    number: 117
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Passport stamps
    idea: The dashboard is an open passport, with a holder page for the user and contents, and a visa page where each project is an inked entry stamp whose shape and mark give its status.
    base: light
    palette:
        table: #e7e5ea, the page behind the book
        cover: #3a2a4a, the thin book edge, decorative only
        visaPaper: #eef3ee, pages under the guilloche
        securityTeal: #1d5f63, guilloche lines at 10 percent, microprint and section labels
        ink: #1d2833, text and the machine readable lines
        muted: #4a5662, field keys, times and last week
        violetInk: #5a2a86, the primary button, the current page, this week and focus
        greenInk: #1f6340, the round On track stamp with a tick
        blueInk: #1f4b8f, the double framed At risk stamp with a triangle
        redInk: #a1262c, the leaf shaped Behind stamp with a crossed square and the overdue notice
    type:
        Three stacks. Serif is Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino,
        URW Palladio L, Georgia, serif. OCR is OCR B, OCR-B, Consolas,
        Lucida Console, monospace. Stamp is Arial Black, Arial, sans-serif
        in caps. Sizes are 30px serif greeting, 30 to 34px bold OCR figures,
        14px black caps stamp titles, 15px bold OCR caps field values, 15 to
        16px serif body and 10 to 13px OCR caps keys and labels.
    layout:
        A dark thin cover frames a two page spread, a narrow holder page on
        the left and a wide visa page on the right, with shaded gutters
        where they meet. Both pages carry a guilloche of overlapping fine
        rings. The holder page has a microprint band, a compass rose mark
        with the spaced caps brand, a hatched photo box with MO, Surname,
        Given name and Date fields, the greeting and date, a tilted red
        notice reading Overdue, 4 tasks are overdue, and the navigation as a
        Contents list with dotted leaders and page numbers. Two machine
        readable lines sit at its foot and folio numbers mark the corners.
        The visa page has the underlined search, a violet pill New project
        button, a round bell and the user, then four teal outlined boxes
        for the figures, then six entry stamps on a loose three column grid,
        each turned 3 to 6 degrees. A stamp holds the project name, team
        between rules, a big percent, tasks and due date, and a status pill.
        Its outline is the status, round with an inner ring for On track,
        a 6px double frame for At risk and a leaf with 28px and 6px corners
        for Behind. Below the spread a second spread holds a lollipop chart
        of ink circles on stems, grey last week and violet this week, and
        an Observations list. Below 820px pages stack, and below 560px the
        stamps go one per row, alternating left and right.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 28 to 32px page margins, 18 to 20px between stamps.
    density: Medium and scattered. Stamps sit loosely on a grid, each turned slightly.
    corners: Book 14px, pages 8px, summary boxes 6px. Stamp outlines follow the status shapes described above.
    borders: 3px ink frames, 6px double for At risk, hairline teal for summary boxes and observation rules.
    shadows: Only the gutter, an inset shade where the pages meet, and a soft drop under the book.
    icons:
        Solid ink marks, a tick for On track, a filled triangle for At
        risk, a crossed filled square for Behind and a clock for overdue,
        each beside the caps word. A compass rose emblem.
    focus: A 2px violet outline offset 3px with a soft violet halo.
    tone: Travel document words, such as Contents, Entries, Observations and Given name.
